msgctxt "27\t89"
msgid "On to our next story..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "117\t373"
msgid ""
"A key figure in the liberal push for Okinawa\\nmilitary expansion, Defense "
"Minister Ryuzo Tamiya,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "374\t579"
msgid ""
"and the man in charge of the Okinawa resort deal\\ncurrently underway, Land "
"Minister Yoshinobu Suzuki,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "580\t697"
msgid "both paid a visit to the embattled region today."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "708\t974"
msgid ""
"On one side is Tamiya-san, a proponent of the island's\\nnewly proposed BMD,"
" or ballistic missile defense system."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1009\t1199"
msgid ""
"While on the other is Suzuki-san, who has long opposed\\nexpansion of "
"American military presence on Okinawan shores."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1200\t1373"
msgid ""
"He suggests that the government instead focus its efforts\\non a new resort "
"which will drive tourism to the region."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1380\t1574"
msgid ""
"Political and business leaders alike are paying close\\nattention to just "
"what these two men's visits will entail."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1594\t1757"
msgid ""
"Tamiya-san's journey got off to a rocky start as he\\nwas greeted at the "
"airport by throngs of protesters..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1758\t1907"
msgid ""
"Carrying signs and handing out flyers opposing\\nhis proposed military "
"expansion plans."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1908\t2028"
msgid ""
"Suzuki-san, on the other hand, was met by\\na faction of local businessmen "
"and financiers,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2029\t2192"
msgid ""
"who proceeded to take him on a personal guided tour\\nof the intended site "
"for his forthcoming resort."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2219\t2365"
msgid ""
"The two proposals, Tamiya-san's military expansion\\ndeal and Suzuki-san's "
"plan for a new resort,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2366\t2485"
msgid ""
"have been met with mixed opinions from\\nthe people of Okinawa. Needless to "
"say..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2486\t2624"
msgid ""
"Both ministers will need to compromise\\nif they hope to accomplish their "
"goals."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2639\t2835"
msgid ""
"Of course, it's clear that this BMD system is vital\\nto ensuring Japan has "
"a bright, stable future."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "2845\t3056"
msgid ""
"But I won't let us keep forcing Okinawa to sacrifice\\nits own well-being "
"for the country's defense."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3057\t3256"
msgid ""
"My resort development plan will help promote tourism\\nto the island and "
"dramatically stimulate its economy,"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3257\t3452"
msgid ""
"thus creating new jobs and opportunities for the humble\\npeople of this "
"beautiful land. I say, Okinawa first."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3465\t3616"
msgid ""
"Defending our home is all that concerns me.\\nI have nothing more to say on "
"the matter."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3617\t3747"
msgid "As opposed to the seemingly\\nmore receptive Suzuki-san..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3750\t3918"
msgid ""
"Tamiya-san departed the airport clearly\\nuninterested in entertaining "
"interviews."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "3929\t4183"
msgid ""
"The unannounced nature of the two ministers' visits\\nhas fueled speculation"
" that both men will attempt to..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4184\t4384"
msgid ""
"Push their respective proposals through the National Diet\\nat some point in"
" the coming weeks and months."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4385\t4482"
msgid "And what do the locals think of all this?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4507\t4593"
msgid "We're crawling with\\nAmerican soldiers as is."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4594\t4707"
msgid "But a resort? Now that's something\\nI might be able to get behind."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4708\t4871"
msgid ""
"Even if someone does go and shoot missiles at us,\\nI'd be willing to bet "
"it'd be at Tokyo, not Okinawa."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "4872\t5012"
msgid ""
"Guess I'm not surprised Tamiya-san's not really\\nthinkin' about what's best"
" for us, though."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "5061\t5332"
msgid ""
"As aspiring prime minister candidates, both men are\\nlikely to be under "
"intense scrutiny for some time now."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "5367\t5434"
msgid "In other news..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "5587\t5733"
msgid "Uncle Kaz... Is that why they keep\\ntrying to kick us out?"
msgstr ""
